{"agent":"ci-admit","data":{"by":"ci-admit","evidence":{"diff_stat":{"deletions":62,"files":15,"insertions":505,"untracked":5},"note":"CLAIM: recorded ci gates can predict a selected run's wall time well enough to decide the suite slot; no per-test durations are stored (git grep: only pytest --durations as an ignored flag), but each ci gate records elapsed_s, waited_s, ci_scope.selected/always_s/ran/workers. MECHANISM: rate = (elapsed - waited - always_s) * workers / selected files; predicted = median(rate) * files / WK.compute(cfg, files).n, so load enters through the one governor. FALSIFIER: a per-run rate predicts no better than a constant, or a small unloaded run still predicts heavy. PROBE 1 (backtest of 200 recorded selected runs with a worker count, each predicted from up to 200 earlier ones, median/p90 relative error): constant 0.35/2.18, global rate 0.29/1.19, per-file attribution 0.28/1.11. Per-file is no better, so the global rate is used. PROBE 2 (real code on the real log: 6059 ci events, 200 measured, newest 50 median 184.2 worker-s/file, scan 0.6 ms; 192 cores): load/core 0.05: 3f 184s, 55f 211s, 100f 384s stay off the slot, 178f 683s takes it; 0.6: 55f 362s, 78f 513s stay, 100f 658s takes it; 0.75 and over: n=1, 3f 552s stays, 24f+ takes it. Falsifier not met. Default 600 s: selected wall p90 531 s, recorded full suite about 2000 s.","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 e5e7fae6d28e63276fa10281c2614fbc95949cd7","ddflow/api/cirun.py":"100644 0f720edbfbddc03e5e1e644ceac6156e1a93451d","ddflow/config_sections/ci.py":"100644 c400fe2a2eecb21c210a739fc4ba9677ce31ec22","ddflow/services/ci/admission.py":"100644 f444923830c5dae11ed033303f5f24b7ee4e5d85","ddflow/services/ci/runner.py":"100644 6cc6ccc0bfa585bc6a0e98a257f94e13fc8427e4","ddflow/services/ci_scope.py":"100644 d54e5290aa09cff11ac913b6df68d1c3e61ddc99","ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.ci.selected_lock_min_runs.toml":"100644 4acd09986625d8edd97bd944f980ad842295c9cb","ddflow/templates/up